      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct to be concerned; a textbook SQL injection with full database access potential is a \"fix it now or lose everything\" scenario where waiting guarantees a catastrophic data breach. While a WAF can deflect traffic, it cannot patch the logic flaw that will be trivial for a skilled attacker to bypass or escalate. The risk of legal penalties, customer churn, and regulatory mandates for notification far outweighs the cost of a brief, scheduled outage to deploy the fix immediately.\n\nTherefore, do not wait for an exploit to confirm the threat; the signature is definitive evidence of exploitable code. You must treat this as a critical incident and activate an emergency patching protocol to maintain both security and compliance.",
